From: PlayThing builder <builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] settings: TV UI mode action bar, and no search bar without Settings Intelligence

1. The PlayThing image declares android.hardware.type.television, so that
   DiPlay drives the CarPlay knob from DPAD keys. In that UI mode the Settings
   window has no action bar, and SettingsActivity.onCreate threw a
   NullPointerException at findViewById(R.id.action_bar).setVisibility(View.GONE):
   the main Settings screen did not open. Skip the call when the view
   is missing.
2. The search bar on the main page starts the search UI in Settings Intelligence
   (com.android.settings.intelligence), which the image does not have, so a tap
   crashed Settings with ActivityNotFoundException. Hide the
   search bar when no activity handles the search intent.

Both changes are in one patch: as two patches with neighbouring lines, the
already-applied check of scripts/aosp-patches.sh failed for the first one.

---
diff --git a/src/com/android/settings/SettingsActivity.java b/src/com/android/settings/SettingsActivity.java
index 00cf069..d263636 100644
--- a/src/com/android/settings/SettingsActivity.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/SettingsActivity.java
@@ -65,6 +65,7 @@ import com.android.settings.dashboard.DashboardFeatureProvider;
 import com.android.settings.dashboard.DashboardSummary;
 import com.android.settings.overlay.FeatureFactory;
 import com.android.settings.search.DeviceIndexFeatureProvider;
+import com.android.settings.search.SearchFeatureProvider;
 import com.android.settings.wfd.WifiDisplaySettings;
 import com.android.settings.widget.SwitchBar;
 import com.android.settingslib.core.instrumentation.Instrumentable;
@@ -299,9 +300,23 @@ public class SettingsActivity extends SettingsDrawerActivity
 
         final boolean deviceProvisioned = Utils.isDeviceProvisioned(this);
         if (mIsShowingDashboard) {
-            findViewById(R.id.search_bar).setVisibility(
-                    deviceProvisioned ? View.VISIBLE : View.INVISIBLE);
-            findViewById(R.id.action_bar).setVisibility(View.GONE);
+            // PlayThing: the search UI is in Settings Intelligence, which the image does not
+            // have, so a tap on the search bar crashed Settings (ActivityNotFoundException). Hide
+            // the search bar when no activity handles the search intent.
+            final SearchFeatureProvider searchProvider =
+                    FeatureFactory.getFactory(this).getSearchFeatureProvider();
+            final boolean searchAvailable = getPackageManager().resolveActivity(
+                    new Intent(SearchFeatureProvider.SEARCH_UI_INTENT)
+                            .setPackage(searchProvider.getSettingsIntelligencePkgName()),
+                    0) != null;
+            findViewById(R.id.search_bar).setVisibility(!searchAvailable ? View.GONE
+                    : deviceProvisioned ? View.VISIBLE : View.INVISIBLE);
+            // PlayThing: in the television UI mode (the knob feature) the window has no
+            // action bar, and this line threw a NullPointerException.
+            final View actionBar = findViewById(R.id.action_bar);
+            if (actionBar != null) {
+                actionBar.setVisibility(View.GONE);
+            }
             final Toolbar toolbar = findViewById(R.id.search_action_bar);
             FeatureFactory.getFactory(this).getSearchFeatureProvider()
                     .initSearchToolbar(this, toolbar);
